           <svg width="48" height="48" viewbox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" style="margin: 0 auto 0.5rem; display: block;"><rect x="4" y="8" width="40" height="32" rx="2" stroke="rgba(242,169,0,.4)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" /> <circle cx="16" cy="20" r="4" stroke="rgba(242,169,0,.4)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" /> <path d="M4 32l12-8 8 6 12-10 8 6" stroke="rgba(242,169,0,.4)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" />
           </svg>
           <p style="color: var(--syd-gold); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; margin: 0;">📷 Paste Image Here</p>
          </div>
         </div>
         <p style="color: var(--syd-gold); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: center; font-style: italic; margin: 0;">Edwin Smith Papyrus</p>
        </div><!-- Key Discovery Box 2 -->
        <div class="content-box" style="padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);">
         <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75rem;"><span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">⚖️</span>
          <div>
           <h3 style="font-weight: bold; color: var(--syd-gold); font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; line-height: 1.4;">The Weighing of the Heart</h3>
           <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.75rem;">In the Ancient world, the heart was seen as a recorder of deeds, determining one's fate after death through its weighing against a feather.</p>
           <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">The Egyptians believed the heart was the centre of the cardiovascular system and connected to other organs through which it received water and air.</p>
          </div>
         </div>
        </div><!-- Image Placeholder 2 -->
        <div style="background: rgba(242,169,0,.08); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(242,169,0,.15);">
