        <svg width="24" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--syd-gold)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" />
        </svg>
       </div></button> <!-- Expandable Content -->
      <div id="greece-content" class="card-expand">
       <div style="padding: 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;"><!-- Classical Greece -->
        <div class="content-box" style="padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);">
         <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75rem;"><span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">👨‍⚕️</span>
          <div>
           <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-weight: bold; color: var(--syd-gold); font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4;">Classical Greece</h3><span class="info-label" style="font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 9999px;">5th Century BCE</span>
           </div>
           <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;"><strong>Hippocrates</strong>, known as the "Father of Medicine," wrote early descriptions of the heart. He identified its basic structure and introduced the idea of two ventricles and two auricles, shaping future medical understanding.</p>
          </div>
         </div>
        </div><!-- Hellenistic Period -->
        <div class="content-box" style="padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);">
         <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75rem;"><span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">🔬</span>
          <div>
           <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-weight: bold; color: var(--syd-gold); font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4;">Hellenistic Period</h3><span class="info-label" style="font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 9999px;">335–280 BCE</span>
           </div>
           <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;"><strong>Herophilus</strong> was the first to recognise that the heart has four chambers.</p>
           <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;"><strong>Erasistratus</strong> described the heart's valves in detail, even naming some based on their shape (like "sigmoid").</p>
          </div>
         </div>
        </div><!-- Image Placeholder -->
